<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net10.0-android;net10.0-ios;net10.0-maccatalyst</TargetFrameworks>
		<TargetFrameworks Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('windows'))">$(TargetFrameworks);net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <!--<TargetFrameworks Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('osx'))">$(TargetFrameworks);net10.0-maccatalyst</TargetFrameworks>-->
		<!-- Uncomment to also build the tizen app. You will need to install tizen by following this: https://github.com/Samsung/Tizen.NET -->
		<!-- <TargetFrameworks>$(TargetFrameworks);net10.0-tizen</TargetFrameworks> -->
		<UseMaui>true</UseMaui>
		<SingleProject>true</SingleProject>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!--Currently the package uses reflection which is not AOT/trimmable compatible-->
    <!--Also iOS release builds fail when this is set to true-->
    <IsAotCompatible>false</IsAotCompatible>
    <IsTrimmable>false</IsTrimmable>
    <PublishTrimmed>false</PublishTrimmed>

		<SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'ios'">15.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
		<SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'maccatalyst'">15.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
		<SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'android'">21.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
		<SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'windows'">10.0.17763.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
		<TargetPlatformMinVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'windows'">10.0.17763.0</TargetPlatformMinVersion>
		<SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'tizen'">6.5</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
	</PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="NugetProperties">
    <Authors>Kebechet</Authors>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Kebechet.Maui.Health</PackageId>
    <Description>Android Health Connect and iOS HealthKit wrapper. Read/write health data including steps, weight, heart rate, workouts, and more. Live workout tracking with pause/resume and automatic duplicate detection.</Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Maui.Health</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Maui.Health</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <DebugSymbols>true</DebugSymbols>
    <DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v7.0.0 — permission requests report every permission, and aggregated reads can skip the permission screen.

BREAKING CHANGES
• Aggregated reads: GetAggregatedHealthData, ByInterval and ByCalendarPeriod take shouldCheckPermissions before the CancellationToken; pass a token by name.
• RequestPermissionResult.DeniedPermissions lists HealthPermissionDto instead of platform permission strings.
• HealthPermissionStatus: iOS reads are Undisclosed and unreadable statuses are Unavailable; NotDetermined now means an unasked iOS write only.
• Android: refused full-history or background access no longer fails RequestPermissions; see FullHistoryReadStatus and BackgroundReadStatus.
• RequestPermissions reports an exception as RequestPermissionError.UnexpectedException.
• PermissionType.Read is 1 and Write 2, so the flags combine: a write-only permission no longer asks for read access too.

NEW
• shouldCheckPermissions: false on aggregated reads fails a read with a missing permission instead of opening the permission screen.
• RequestPermissionResult reports PermissionStatuses for every requested permission, so no GetPermissionStatuses call is needed after a request.
• RequestPermissionResult.IsPermissionScreenShown tells a refusal apart from a platform that declined to ask again.
• OpenPermissionSettings opens Health Connect's permission screen for the app (Android).

FIXED
• Android: parallel permission requests run one after another instead of leaving invisible activities that swallow every tap.
• GetPermissionStatuses never throws; without a current activity or Health Connect it reports Unavailable.

PREVIOUS RELEASE — v6.0.0: the health data types move to Kebechet.Types.Health, a package without MAUI, under its own namespaces.

BREAKING CHANGES
• Namespaces (#62): DTOs, enums, results and their helpers are now in Kebechet.Types.Health.* — replace using Maui.Health.Models with using Kebechet.Types.Health.Models (same for .Enums, .Extensions, .Constants).

NEW
• Kebechet.Types.Health (#62): the DTOs, enums and results as a plain .NET package, for code shared with a watch app or a backend.
• HealthDataSdk.GoogleHealthServices (#62): marks workouts recorded on a Wear OS watch with Health Services.

CHANGED
• WorkoutSession (#62): its constructor and the DTO-to-permission helpers are public, so other health libraries can use them.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Maui.Controls" Version="$(MauiVersion)" />
		<PackageReference Include="UnitsNet" Version="5.75.0" />
	</ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Types.Health\Types.Health.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0-android'">
	  <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Health.Connect.ConnectClient" Version="1.1.0.2" />

    <!--Health.Connect.ConnectClient pulls in newer AndroidX deps (Activity 1.12.x, Lifecycle 2.10.x, SavedState 1.4.x)
        but MAUI's transitive *.Ktx packages have tight version constraints expecting older versions-->
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Activity.Ktx" VersionOverride="1.12.4.1" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.LiveData" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.LiveData.Core" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.LiveData.Core.Ktx" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.Process" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.Runtime.Ktx" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.Runtime.Ktx.Android" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Lifecycle.ViewModel.Ktx" VersionOverride="2.10.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.SavedState.SavedState.Ktx" VersionOverride="1.4.0.2" NoWarn="NU1608" />

    <!--Fragment.Ktx 1.8.8 bug requires this: https://github.com/dotnet/android-libraries/issues/1186-->
    <!--https://github.com/dotnet/android-libraries/issues/1181#issuecomment-3053297891-->
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.SavedState" VersionOverride="1.4.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Fragment.Ktx" VersionOverride="1.8.9" />
	</ItemGroup>


  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>

    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>

    <None Include="..\..\icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
